  "schemaVersion": 4,
  "id": "t02-009",
  "track": "track-02",
  "title": "Microsoft.Extensions.Logging levels providers filters scopes and source generation",
  "status": "source-backed-scope-complete",
  "inventoryComplete": true,
  "concepts": [
    "Logging records an event with a category, severity, event identity, message template, values, and optional exception. A provider decides where an enabled event goes; filtering decides which events reach each provider.",
    "Structured message templates preserve named values for querying. Interpolated strings usually format eagerly and discard this structured shape. For hot paths, LoggerMessage source generation reduces repeated parsing and allocations while preserving event meaning.",
    "A logging scope attaches shared context to a bounded operation and is visible only through providers that support scopes. It is correlation context, not a transaction, security boundary, or replacement for trace context.",
    "Provider/category filters select one rule per provider and category using provider name/alias, longest matching category prefix, and last rule among ties; the minimum level is the fallback. Environment configuration and code both affect logging, so diagnose the effective provider and rule instead of assuming that a missing event means its call site did not run."
  ],
