  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": ".NET 11 GA checked 2026-11-20",
      "items": [
        "Use the .NET 11 documentation and package reference as the current baseline. Logging abstractions, provider packages, and source-generator surfaces can ship on independent package versions; explain the package version being used rather than assuming every app targets the runtime's bundled copy.",
        "LoggerMessage source generation is the current high-performance built-in pattern; traditional ILogger extension methods remain valid and simpler for low-volume code. .NET 11 adds generic source-generated logging methods; the C# 13 allows ref struct anti-constraint remains unsupported."
